usage: hep-genesis-agent [-h] [--project NAME] [--project-dir PATH]
                         [--servers SPEC] [--output-dir PATH]
                         [--resume RUN_ID] [--temperature TEMPERATURE]
                         [--list-projects] [--archive-project] [--coding]
                         [--coding-auto] [--link-codebase PATH_OR_GIT_URL]
                         [--list-codebases] [--quick] [--chat NAME] [--report]
                         [--max-rounds MAX_ROUNDS] [--list-chats]
                         [--no-extras] [--list-skills] [--max-waves N]
                         [--workers N] [--max-tool-calls N] [--wall-clock MIN]
                         [--approve] [--auto] [--allow-hpc]
                         [--steer RUN_ID TEXT] [--pause RUN_ID]
                         [--stop RUN_ID] [--continue DIRECTION_ID]
                         [--list-runs] [--board] [--show-run RUN_ID]
                         [--events {jsonl}] [--no-research-tools]
                         [query]

Headless agent runner: the CLI twin of the desktop app's chat.

Two modes, like the desktop app:

* research (default): deep, multi-direction research on a shared board —
  survey -> plan -> critic -> (approval) -> waves of parallel direction
  workers -> critic -> replan or stop -> report -> honesty pass
  (``docs/research-engine.md``). The budget — ``--max-waves``, ``--workers``,
  ``--max-tool-calls``, ``--wall-clock`` (defaults 4 / 5 / 200 / 120 min, or
  ``HEP_RESEARCH_*`` in the environment) — bounds it; steer a running run
  with ``--steer``, pause/resume it, continue an open direction of the
  report with ``--continue``.
* ``--quick``: one tool-calling assistant over a persistent chat
  (``<project>/chats/<name>.json``); follow-up queries keep their context,
  long chats auto-compact, and ``--report`` (or asking for a report in the
  query) writes the LaTeX/PDF report of the whole chat.

Both run inside a research project directory that collects outputs,
dispatched-job artifacts, resume state, and provenance — the same on-disk
layout the desktop app uses (see ``hep_genesis.projects``).

LLM configuration comes from the environment: ``LLM_URL``, ``LLM_MODEL``,
``LLM_API_KEY`` (+ optional per-stage ``LLM_{SURVEY,PLAN,WORKER,CRITIC,
REPORT,QUICK}_*`` overrides — see ``agent/llm_factory.py``).

positional arguments:
  query                 the research question / task

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --project NAME        project name or slug; created if missing
  --project-dir PATH    explicit project directory (overrides --project)
  --servers SPEC        MCP server: module:<python.module>, command:<exe
                        args>, the URL of a running streamable-http server
                        (…/mcp), a local path, or a git URL to install; prefix
                        name= to name it (repeatable); default: the three
                        bundled servers; 'none' for no servers
  --output-dir PATH     override the run output dir
  --resume RUN_ID       resume a paused or failed research run (a query of
                        just 'continue'/'resume' resumes the --project's
                        latest stopped run)
  --temperature TEMPERATURE
  --list-projects       list projects and exit
  --archive-project     move --project (its chats and outputs) to
                        old_experiments/, where it is permanently deleted
                        after 90 days, and exit
  --coding              enable the last-resort run_coding_task tool (pi
                        harness; all code is saved under the project)
  --coding-auto         quick mode with --coding: skip the per-task approval
                        prompt (research mode never prompts: enabling coding
                        is the approval)
  --link-codebase PATH_OR_GIT_URL
                        link an existing codebase to --project so coding tasks
                        can build on it (local folder in place, git URL
                        shallow-cloned + SHA-pinned); repeatable, exits after
                        linking when no query is given
  --list-codebases      list the --project's linked codebases and exit
  --quick               quick mode: one tool-calling assistant over a
                        persistent chat (follow-ups keep context; see --chat)
  --chat NAME           quick mode: chat name within the project (default:
                        'default')
  --report              write the LaTeX/PDF report of the --chat (after the
                        query, if one is given)
  --max-rounds MAX_ROUNDS
                        quick mode: tool-call rounds per turn (default 30)
  --list-chats          list the --project's chats and exit
  --no-extras           quick mode: don't bind load_skill/remember or read the
                        workspace (HEP_WORKSPACE_DIR, default ~/HEP-Genesis:
                        skills/*.md + MEMORY.md)
  --list-skills         list workspace skills and exit

research mode:
  --max-waves N         research budget: waves of directions (default 4)
  --workers N           research budget: directions run in parallel (default
                        5)
  --max-tool-calls N    research budget: total tool calls, survey excluded
                        (default 400)
  --wall-clock MIN      research budget: wall clock in minutes (default 120)
  --approve             show the planned directions and ask before executing
                        (edit/approve/reject)
  --auto                never ask: approve the plan as proposed (default when
                        stdin is not a TTY)
  --allow-hpc           allow HPC dispatch (facility allocation) without
                        asking; never implied by --auto
  --steer RUN_ID TEXT   append a steering note to a running research run and
                        exit
  --pause RUN_ID        ask a running research run to pause at its next check
  --stop RUN_ID         ask a running research run to stop and write its
                        report
  --continue DIRECTION_ID
                        start a new run on the same board continuing this open
                        direction (see the report)
  --list-runs           list the --project's research runs and exit
  --board               print the --chat's research board (directions,
                        findings with evidence, critiques, open directions)
                        and exit
  --show-run RUN_ID     print a run's record and its last events, and exit
  --events {jsonl}      also print every run event as JSON lines on stdout
  --no-research-tools   do not bind the built-in web/arXiv research tools to
                        workers

server SPECs (repeatable --servers; omitted = the three bundled servers
hep-research-aid, alcf-tools and nersc-tools, the app's defaults; "none" = no servers):
  module:hep_genesis.domain.mcp_server   pre-installed python module (-m)
  command:uvx duckduckgo-mcp-server      pre-installed executable + args
  emulators=http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp   running streamable-http server, connected by URL (name= optional)
  /path/to/repo | https://github.com/... pip-installed, then run by name

environment:
  LLM_URL, LLM_MODEL, LLM_API_KEY        chat endpoint (OpenAI-compatible)
  LLM_API_KEY=chatgpt                    pay with your ChatGPT Plus/Pro plan instead of a key
                                         (LLM_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1; sign in once with
                                         hep-genesis-chatgpt-auth; --models lists the slugs)
  LLM_SURVEY_*/LLM_PLAN_*/LLM_WORKER_*/LLM_CRITIC_*/LLM_REPORT_*   per-stage overrides
  LLM_CODER_*                            coding-harness model (with --coding; chatgpt works too)
  HEP_PROJECTS_DIR                       project root (default ~/hep-genesis/projects)
  HEP_CODING=1                           same as --coding
  HEP_WORKSPACE_DIR                      skills/*.md + MEMORY.md (default ~/HEP-Genesis)
  HEP_PI_BIN                             explicit path to the pi binary
  HEP_RESEARCH_MAX_WAVES / _WORKERS / _MAX_TOOL_CALLS / _WALL_CLOCK_MIN   research budget defaults

examples:
  hep-genesis-agent --list-projects
  hep-genesis-agent --archive-project --project qcd-eos     # move to old_experiments/ (90-day purge)
  hep-genesis-agent "compute a test power spectrum" --project qcd-eos \
      --servers module:hep_genesis.domain.mcp_server        # research mode, default budget
  hep-genesis-agent "..." --project qcd-eos --max-waves 6 --wall-clock 240 --approve --servers ...
  hep-genesis-agent --steer RUN_ID "also compare against the Planck value" --project qcd-eos
  hep-genesis-agent --pause RUN_ID --project qcd-eos ;  hep-genesis-agent --resume RUN_ID --project qcd-eos
  hep-genesis-agent --continue d-04 --project qcd-eos --servers ...   # a report's open direction
  hep-genesis-agent --board --project qcd-eos                 # the chat's board: findings, evidence, critiques
  hep-genesis-agent --show-run RUN_ID --project qcd-eos       # run record + last events
  hep-genesis-agent --report --project qcd-eos                # PDF of the chat (quick + research turns)
  hep-genesis-agent --quick "list the emulators you have" --project qcd-eos \
      --servers module:hep_genesis.domain.mcp_server        # chat 'default'
  hep-genesis-agent --quick "now plot P(k) for the first one" --project qcd-eos \
      --servers module:hep_genesis.domain.mcp_server        # follow-up, same chat
  hep-genesis-agent --report --project qcd-eos                # PDF of that chat
  hep-genesis-agent --project qcd-eos --link-codebase ~/code/my-analysis
  hep-genesis-agent "fit the slope of the downloaded HMF" --project qcd-eos \
      --coding --servers module:hep_genesis.domain.mcp_server
